From 459abae601411d191a1f4c99fe55b60d59e59305 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] server: share avatar AV driver for external AudioChunk ingress

Keep CyberVerse as the sole avatar/lip-sync/AV pacing/LiveKit publisher while
allowing already-synthesized AudioChunk streams to enter the same internal AV
driver used by standard TTS. The ingress is session scoped, sequence checked,
fail-closed, and torn down with the CyberVerse session. Yance gains no WebRTC,
JWT-signing, avatar, lip-sync, resampling, or AV-pacing authority.
---
